{
  "verso": "1.1",
  "metadata": {
    "defaultKernel": "powershell",
    "activeLayout": {
      "extensionId": "verso.layout.notebook",
      "layoutId": "notebook"
    }
  },
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "52433ee0-72cc-4894-b215-586c24679f48",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "# RuleOne Financial Analysis Notebook\n\nThis notebook queries SEC EDGAR data from SQLite and visualizes financial metrics, using both F# and PowerShell in the Verso Notebook extension (see [ADR-0004](../docs/adr/ADR-0004-notebook-polyglot-language-strategy.md)):\n\n- **F#** cells query and shape the data, calling directly into the \u0060RuleOne.ETL\u0060 and \u0060RuleOne.Analytics\u0060 libraries.\n- **PowerShell** cells handle orchestration: rendering charts, opening files, and calling the already-built \u0060RuleOne\u0060 PowerShell module.\n\nAll cells share one variable store, so values flow between languages without manual hand-off."
    },
    {
      "id": "af1aa2ce-4a91-49cf-8184-265cdbbad773",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "fsharp",
      "source": "// Reference the RuleOne assemblies and SQLite provider built by \u0060dotnet build\u0060.\n// Paths assume the notebook runs with the repository root as the working directory.\n#r \u0022src/RuleOne.ETL/bin/Debug/net8.0/SQLitePCLRaw.core.dll\u0022\n#r \u0022src/RuleOne.ETL/bin/Debug/net8.0/SQLitePCLRaw.provider.e_sqlite3.dll\u0022\n#r \u0022src/RuleOne.ETL/bin/Debug/net8.0/SQLitePCLRaw.batteries_v2.dll\u0022\n#r \u0022src/RuleOne.ETL/bin/Debug/net8.0/Microsoft.Data.Sqlite.dll\u0022\n#r \u0022src/RuleOne.Analytics/bin/Debug/net8.0/RuleOne.Analytics.dll\u0022\n#r \u0022src/RuleOne.ETL/bin/Debug/net8.0/RuleOne.ETL.dll\u0022\n\nopen RuleOne.ETL\nopen RuleOne.Analytics\n\nSQLitePCL.Batteries.Init()\n\nlet repoRoot = System.IO.Directory.GetCurrentDirectory()\nlet dbPath = System.IO.Path.Combine(repoRoot, \u0022ruleone.db\u0022)\nlet connectionString = sprintf \u0022Data Source=%s\u0022 dbPath\n\nprintfn \u0022Using database at %s\u0022 connectionString"
    },
    {
      "id": "a22aaea0-a66f-49e4-ade0-4f82dc8caf8c",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Query Revenue and Earnings (F#)\n\nCall \u0060RuleOne.ETL.Database.queryFactsByConcept\u0060 directly rather than re-implementing SQLite access."
    },
    {
      "id": "ba1b9799-850d-4fd6-ab6f-a2a294fd3774",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "fsharp",
      "source": "let revenueFacts = Database.queryFactsByConcept connectionString \u0022Revenues\u0022\nlet earningsFacts = Database.queryFactsByConcept connectionString \u0022NetIncome\u0022\n\nprintfn \u0022Found %d revenue records and %d earnings records\u0022 revenueFacts.Length earningsFacts.Length\n\nrevenueFacts\n|\u003E List.truncate 5\n|\u003E List.iter (fun f -\u003E\n    printfn \u0022%s - %s: $%s\u0022\n        (defaultArg f.CompanyName \u0022Unknown\u0022)\n        (defaultArg f.Period \u0022Unknown\u0022)\n        (defaultArg f.Value \u00220\u0022))"
    },
    {
      "id": "3a8ee6ba-845c-46cc-8a86-bd4e27562605",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Shape Data and Calculate CAGR (F#)\n\nShape the raw facts into chartable records and calculate CAGR using \u0060RuleOne.Analytics.FinancialMetrics\u0060, leveraging F#\u0027s records and option types."
    },
    {
      "id": "59310437-1fc2-4262-8d5d-594a583fe4e4",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "fsharp",
      "source": "type ChartPoint = { Period: string; ValueMillions: decimal }\n\nlet toMillions (value: string option) =\n    match value |\u003E Option.bind (fun v -\u003E\n        match System.Decimal.TryParse v with\n        | true, parsed -\u003E Some parsed\n        | false, _ -\u003E None) with\n    | Some parsed -\u003E parsed / 1_000_000m\n    | None -\u003E 0m\n\nlet revenueData =\n    revenueFacts\n    |\u003E List.map (fun f -\u003E { Period = defaultArg f.Period \u0022Unknown\u0022; ValueMillions = toMillions f.Value })\n    |\u003E List.sortBy (fun r -\u003E r.Period)\n\nlet earningsData =\n    earningsFacts\n    |\u003E List.map (fun f -\u003E { Period = defaultArg f.Period \u0022Unknown\u0022; ValueMillions = toMillions f.Value })\n    |\u003E List.sortBy (fun r -\u003E r.Period)\n\nlet revenueCagr =\n    if revenueData.Length \u003E= 2 then\n        let first = revenueData.[0].ValueMillions\n        let last = revenueData.[revenueData.Length - 1].ValueMillions\n        let years = decimal (revenueData.Length - 1)\n        FinancialMetrics.calculateCAGR first last years\n    else\n        None\n\nmatch revenueCagr with\n| Some cagr -\u003E printfn \u0022Revenue CAGR: %.2f%%\u0022 (cagr * 100m)\n| None -\u003E printfn \u0022Unable to calculate CAGR (need at least two periods of positive values)\u0022"
    },
    {
      "id": "d9b37e06-81ce-466f-a96f-261e9ff34e5a",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Visualize Revenue Trend (PowerShell)\n\nRendering a chart to a file and opening it is host/OS orchestration, so this uses PowerShell. \u0060$revenueData\u0060 was produced by the F# cells above and is available here through Verso\u0027s shared variable store."
    },
    {
      "id": "e26296b1-73b2-41cc-8e57-558a0d25dcde",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "powershell",
      "source": "$repoRoot = Get-Location\n$chartPath = Join-Path $repoRoot \u0027samples/RevenueTrend.html\u0027\n\n$periodsJson = ($revenueData | ForEach-Object { $_.Period }) | ConvertTo-Json -Compress\n$valuesJson = ($revenueData | ForEach-Object { $_.ValueMillions }) | ConvertTo-Json -Compress\n\n@\u0022\n\u003C!DOCTYPE html\u003E\n\u003Chtml\u003E\n\u003Chead\u003E\n    \u003Cmeta charset=\u0022utf-8\u0022\u003E\n    \u003Ctitle\u003ERevenue Growth Trend\u003C/title\u003E\n    \u003Cscript src=\u0022https://cdn.plot.ly/plotly-2.35.2.min.js\u0022\u003E\u003C/script\u003E\n\u003C/head\u003E\n\u003Cbody\u003E\n    \u003Cdiv id=\u0022chart\u0022 style=\u0022width:1000px;height:600px;\u0022\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\n    \u003Cscript\u003E\n        Plotly.newPlot(\u0027chart\u0027, [{\n            x: $periodsJson,\n            y: $valuesJson,\n            type: \u0027scatter\u0027,\n            mode: \u0027lines\u002Bmarkers\u0027,\n            name: \u0027Revenue\u0027\n        }], {\n            title: \u0027Revenue Growth Trend\u0027,\n            xaxis: { title: \u0027Period\u0027 },\n            yaxis: { title: \u0027Revenue (Millions USD)\u0027 }\n        });\n    \u003C/script\u003E\n\u003C/body\u003E\n\u003C/html\u003E\n\u0022@ | Set-Content -Path $chartPath -Encoding utf8\n\nInvoke-Item $chartPath\nWrite-Output \u0022Chart written to $chartPath\u0022"
    },
    {
      "id": "2237f034-01da-4253-b708-65cef81643e7",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Visualize Revenue and Earnings Together (PowerShell)\n\nCombine \u0060$revenueData\u0060 and \u0060$earningsData\u0060 into one chart."
    },
    {
      "id": "d5730166-a134-4015-9286-60fac406afdd",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "powershell",
      "source": "$repoRoot = Get-Location\n$chartPath = Join-Path $repoRoot \u0027samples/RevenueAndEarningsTrend.html\u0027\n\n$revenuePeriodsJson = ($revenueData | ForEach-Object { $_.Period }) | ConvertTo-Json -Compress\n$revenueValuesJson = ($revenueData | ForEach-Object { $_.ValueMillions }) | ConvertTo-Json -Compress\n$earningsPeriodsJson = ($earningsData | ForEach-Object { $_.Period }) | ConvertTo-Json -Compress\n$earningsValuesJson = ($earningsData | ForEach-Object { $_.ValueMillions }) | ConvertTo-Json -Compress\n\n@\u0022\n\u003C!DOCTYPE html\u003E\n\u003Chtml\u003E\n\u003Chead\u003E\n    \u003Cmeta charset=\u0022utf-8\u0022\u003E\n    \u003Ctitle\u003ERevenue and Earnings Trend\u003C/title\u003E\n    \u003Cscript src=\u0022https://cdn.plot.ly/plotly-2.35.2.min.js\u0022\u003E\u003C/script\u003E\n\u003C/head\u003E\n\u003Cbody\u003E\n    \u003Cdiv id=\u0022chart\u0022 style=\u0022width:1000px;height:600px;\u0022\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\n    \u003Cscript\u003E\n        Plotly.newPlot(\u0027chart\u0027, [\n            { x: $revenuePeriodsJson, y: $revenueValuesJson, type: \u0027scatter\u0027, mode: \u0027lines\u002Bmarkers\u0027, name: \u0027Revenue\u0027 },\n            { x: $earningsPeriodsJson, y: $earningsValuesJson, type: \u0027scatter\u0027, mode: \u0027lines\u002Bmarkers\u0027, name: \u0027Net Income\u0027 }\n        ], {\n            title: \u0027Revenue and Earnings Trend\u0027,\n            xaxis: { title: \u0027Period\u0027 },\n            yaxis: { title: \u0027Amount (Millions USD)\u0027 }\n        });\n    \u003C/script\u003E\n\u003C/body\u003E\n\u003C/html\u003E\n\u0022@ | Set-Content -Path $chartPath -Encoding utf8\n\nInvoke-Item $chartPath\nWrite-Output \u0022Chart written to $chartPath\u0022"
    },
    {
      "id": "48d9517c-1077-4909-b666-3abd322ba41f",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## List Securities via the RuleOne Module (PowerShell)\n\nDemonstrate the other PowerShell role from ADR-0004: calling an already-built, well-established operation \u2014 here, the \u0060RuleOne\u0060 module\u0027s \u0060Get-R1Securities\u0060 (see [ADR-0003](../docs/adr/ADR-0003-powershell-module-design.md)) \u2014 instead of writing new query logic."
    },
    {
      "id": "07b55562-8b8a-476c-97ac-ee2c0d94f386",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "powershell",
      "source": "Import-Module (Join-Path (Get-Location) \u0027modules/RuleOne/RuleOne.psd1\u0027) -Force\n\nGet-R1Securities | Format-Table -AutoSize"
    },
    {
      "id": "c1886910-1cbd-48b5-a9a6-6804caf8f884",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Summary\n\nThis notebook demonstrates:\n- Querying financial facts (revenue, earnings) directly through \u0060RuleOne.ETL.Database\u0060 in F#\n- Shaping data and calculating CAGR through \u0060RuleOne.Analytics\u0060 in F#\n- Visualizing trends using Plotly (rendered as standalone HTML, opened in your browser) in PowerShell\n- Orchestrating an already-built operation (\u0060Get-R1Securities\u0060) through the \u0060RuleOne\u0060 PowerShell module\n\nTo use this notebook:\n1. Build the solution so the referenced assemblies exist: \u0060dotnet build\u0060\n2. Fetch some data: \u0060dotnet run --project src/RuleOne.ETL 0000789019 10-K\u0060\n3. Install the [Verso Notebook](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=Datafication.verso-notebook) extension and open this file with it\n4. Execute cells sequentially from the repository root"
    }
  ]
}